WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.980
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.360
So as you know,  we have a podcast  'Dear Hank and John'

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.080
or as I prefer to think of it 'Dear John and Hank'

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.540
And on that podcast, I recently confessed that instead of pouring milk on my cereal, I use water.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:16.820
Now Nerdfighteria is generally a very supportive community, but their condemnation of my cereal eating habits was swift and nearly universal.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.980
People sent in scientific studies supposedly proving you're supposed to eat cereal with milk

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:26.520
And then there was this vine which recreated one person's experience of eating cereal with water

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.400
But along the way, Hank, I learned there is a secret community of people like me out there.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.440
According to one study, 13% of Americans put coffee in their cereal.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.500
Another 12% use orange juice.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.120
I've even heard of some people who use lemon-lime gatorade

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.400
So today I'm going to taste test all of the ways of moistening cereal.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.240
Which cereal? Well I chose Raisin Bran, because it toes the line between healthy and delicious

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.600
I mean you know it's healthy, because it has 'bran' in the title,

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.220
but you know it's delicious because it has more calories, sugar, and sodium than 'Lucky Charms'.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.380
Speaking of which, I also picked up some Lucky Charms, because it turns out it's healthy.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.100
Okay, first off we have Raisin Bran mixed with delicious, safe American tap water.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.480
Note: only 'safe and delicious' in certain jurisdictions.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.740
Ah, it's so good, I just love Raisin Bran with water, it is delicious.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.340
That is just absolutely magnificent, five raisins.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.140
Next up, we're gonna mix our Raisin Bran with some Florida orange juice.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.460
Oh...No...NO!

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.700
Two great ingredients, that when mixed together just turn out horribly.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.840
For me, the orange juice is one raisin out of five, even that's a little generous.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.720
Ok, up third: Raisin Bran with Lemon Lime Gatorade.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.380
In general, I'm a big Gatorade fan, and because I'd just had the orange juice

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.840
it was so much better by comparison that it was almost "good",

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.080
But it still wasn't good: 2 raisins out of 5.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.740
Fourth up, hot black coffee straight from my AFC Wimbledon mug, into the Raisin Bran!

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.440
I gotta say, for me this tasted almost exclusively like coffee, and not at all like Raisin Bran

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.620
But whatever! I like coffee, and it's fine in bran form. 3 raisins out of 5!

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.840
And then lastly, we have Raisin Bran mixed with cow's milk.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:09.160
Agh! It's just disgusting! It's so rich, it tastes like I'm eating cake or something! I just - That's not Breakfast!

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.540
I'm gonna give milk 2 raisins out of 5.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.120
By the way, Sarah just built a Louvre out of Legos

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.100
And then Henry and I attacked it with a clone army!

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:20.780
So there you have it, Hank. According to a scientific study of my taste buds, the best liquid  to pour on your Raisin Bran is water.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:27.540
Followed in order by coffee, lemon lime Gatorade, that stuff that comes out of the nether regions of a cow,  and orange juice.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.980
Now Hank, you said on the podcast that you tried cereal with water, and you didn't like it - you're a milk guy

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.720
So we have an intractable disagreement.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.260
But I think we're gonna continue to respect each other and collaborate anyway, and there may be a lesson in that.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.200
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

